a rising tide of Islamist militancy in  Africa is a growing threat to the US and  Europe there is a dangerous  misconception that African militant  groups are too locally focused or weak  to pose a real danger Africa is the next  front for the Salafi jihadi movement a  global ideological movement that  includes Isis and al-qaeda African  Salafi jihadi groups provide a local  base and source of resilience for these  organizations they are gaining strength  not because of ideological resonance but  because the spread of insurgencies and  conflict creates opportunities to  insinuate themselves in communities the  Trump administration is trying to do  more against these groups with increased  raids and drone strikes in places like  Somalia but it has still failed to  recognize the link between local  conflicts and grievances in the Salafi  jihadi movement these local issues  conflict and poor governance feel remote  and irrelevant to Americans and the task  of resolving them from Nigeria to Mali  to Libya to Somalia is large but  Americans must understand that  addressing these challenges now is far  cheaper than fighting yet another war  what's your take on American policy in  Africa  let us know in your comments also let us  know what other topics you'd like our  scholars to cover in 60 seconds and be  sure to LIKE and subscribe for more  research and videos from AEI
 

